[1.361, "o", "\u001b[2;58H\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m\u001b[2mstop. The focused block is drawn with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249minverse\u001b[39m or a left bar. A one-line\u001b[3;58Hlegend sits at the bottom:\u001b[7;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m4.\u001b[C\u001b[39m\u001b[2mEnter on a block opens an inline composer under it (an \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mInput\u001b[39m with\u001b[8;58H\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mautoFocus\u001b[39m). The user types a comment and presses Enter. The comment is\u001b[9;58Hpinned under the block, dim, prefixed with a marker. No model call yet.\u001b[10;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m5.\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m\u001b[2ma\u001b[39m on a block opens the same composer in ask mode. Enter sends the\u001b[11;58Hquestion through \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m$.model.fork\u001b[39m with the quoted block as the first line of\u001b[12;58Hthe prompt. The answer streams in under the block. Nothing enters the main\u001b[13;58Htranscript. The exchange is kept on the block and can be turned into a\u001b[14;58Hcomment with one press.\u001b[15;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m6.\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m\u001b[2ms\u001b[39m submits the review. The mod builds one prompt from all pinned comments,\u001b[16;58Heach anchored by heading path and quoted text, and calls\u001b[17;58H\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m$.prompt.submit\u001b[39m. The model revises the document in the main conversation\u001b[18;58Has usual. The pane stays open and refreshes on the next \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mWrite\u001b[39m/\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mEdit\u001b[39m.\u001b[19;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m7.\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m\u001b[2mo\u001b[39m approves: submits the plugin's expected approval phrase (for superpowers,\u001b[20;58H\"Looks good, proceed\") so the plugin's own flow continues.\u001b[22;55H3.2 Why this beats a per-line chat window\u001b[24;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m-\u001b[C\u001b[39m\u001b[2mOne revision pass instead of many partial edits. Cheaper and the document\u001b[25;57Hstays coherent.\u001b[26;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m-\u001b[C\u001b[39m\u001b[2mClarifying questions do not pollute the main context. \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m$.model.fork\u001b[39m reuses\u001b[27;57Hthe cached prefix, so each question costs roughly one short reply.\u001b[28;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m-\u001b[C\u001b[39m\u001b[2mThe user keeps control of when the model acts. Nothing is sent until \u001b[38;2;177;185;249ms\u001b[39m or\u001b[29;57H\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mo\u001b[39m.\u001b[30;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m-\u001b[C\u001b[39m\u001b[2mIt mirrors what people already know from GitHub reviews.\u001b[32;55H3.3 Escalation path per block\u001b[34;55HEvery ask-mode exchange has three exits, drawn as plain Buttons under it:\u001b[36;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m-\u001b[C\u001b[39m\u001b[2mKeep as comment: converts the Q and A into a pinned review comment.\u001b[39;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38mcomment: \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mwhat\u001b[Cshould change here\u001b[Ccancel\u001b[42;3H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
