[0.007, "o", "\u001b[13;1H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m› Prompt from the doc-review plugin\r\n\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m❯ I reviewed DESIGN.md and have 1 comment. Please\u001b[39m \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mrevise the document to address each one, keep \u001b[39m  \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mthe rest as it is, and then summarise what \u001b[39m     \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mchanged per comment.\u001b[39m                            \r\n                                                  \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1. under \"claude-doc-review: a Claude Code mod \u001b[39m \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mfor discussing design and plan documents > 3. \u001b[39m  \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mPrimary UX: review like a pull request, not \u001b[39m    \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mlike a chat > 3.3 Escalation path per block\", \u001b[39m  \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mthe list item beginning \"Send to conversation: \u001b[39m \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m$.prompt.submit right now with the block as \u001b[39m    \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mhidden context, for when the user…\":\u001b[39m            \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m   > Send to conversation: $.prompt.submit \u001b[39m     \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mright now with the block as hidden context, for\u001b[39m \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mwhen the user wants the model to act \u001b[39m           \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mimmediately.\u001b[39m                                    \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m   Comment: Say which block the hidden context \u001b[39m \r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mis, so the model can quote it back.\u001b[39m             \u001b[36;1H\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m·\u001b[CDeciphering… \r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Running multiple Claude sessions? Use \u001b[38;6H/color and /rename to tell them apart at a \u001b[39;6Hglance.\u001b[42;1H❯ \u001b[44;42Hesc to interrupt · ← for agents\u001b[42;3H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.276, "o", "\u001b[2;52H\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m \u001b[2C  \u001b[Cas usual. The pane s\u001b[Cays open and refreshes on the\u001b[Cnext \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mWrite\u001b[39m/\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mEdit\u001b[39m.        \u001b[3;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m7.\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mo\u001b[39m approves: submits the plugin's expected approval phrase (for\u001b[Csuperpowers,\u001b[4;58H\"Looks\u001b[Cgood,\u001b[Cproceed\")\u001b[Cso\u001b[Cthe\u001b[Cplugin's\u001b[Cown\u001b[Cflow\u001b[Ccontinues.\u001b[5;52H \u001b[2C                                         \u001b[6;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m\u001b[1m3.2 Why this beats a per-line chat window\u001b[7;52H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m \u001b[2C \u001b[C   \u001b[C        \u001b[C    \u001b[C       \u001b[C  \u001b[C    \u001b[C       \u001b[C      \u001b[C       \u001b[C   \u001b[C   \u001b[C        \u001b[8;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m-\u001b[COne revision pass\u001b[Cinstead\u001b[Cof\u001b[Cmany\u001b[Cpartial\u001b[Cedits.\u001b[CCheaper\u001b[Cand\u001b[Cthe\u001b[Cdocument\u001b[9;52H \u001b[2C \u001b[Cst\u001b[Cys coherent.     \u001b[C  \u001b[C   \u001b[C       \u001b[C   \u001b[C    \u001b[C        \u001b[C            \u001b[C      \u001b[10;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m-\u001b[CClarifying\u001b[Cqu\u001b[Cstion\u001b[C do not pollute\u001b[Cthe main context.\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m$.model.fork\u001b[C\u001b[39mreuses\u001b[11;52H \u001b[2C \u001b[Ct\u001b[3Ccached prefix, s\u001b[C each ques\u001b[Cion costs roughly one short reply.  \u001b[C \u001b[C  \u001b[12;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m-\u001b[CThe\u001b[Cuser\u001b[Ckeeps\u001b[Ccontrol\u001b[Cof\u001b[Cwhen\u001b[Cthe\u001b[Cmodel\u001b[Cacts.\u001b[CNothing\u001b[Cis\u001b[Csent\u001b[Cuntil\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;177;185;249ms\u001b[C\u001b[39mor\u001b[13;52H \u001b[2C \u001b[C\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mo\u001b[39m.\u001b[C       \u001b[C    \u001b[C      \u001b[C       \u001b[C    \u001b[C    \u001b[C      \u001b[C        \u001b[14;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m-\u001b[CIt\u001b[Cmirrors\u001b[Cwhat\u001b[Cpeople\u001b[Calready\u001b[Cknow\u001b[Cfrom\u001b[CGitHub\u001b[Creviews.\u001b[15;52H \u001b[2C                             \u001b[16;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m\u001b[1m3.3 Escalation path per block\u001b[17;52H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m \u001b[2C     \u001b[C        \u001b[C        \u001b[C   \u001b[C     \u001b[C      \u001b[C     \u001b[C  \u001b[C     \u001b[C       \u001b[C     \u001b[C   \u001b[18;52H\u001b[7m▶\u001b[2C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38mEvery ask-mode exchange has three\u001b[Cexits,\u001b[Cdrawn\u001b[Cas\u001b[Cplain\u001b[CButtons\u001b[Cunder\u001b[Cit:\u001b[19;55H\u001b[38;2;5;162;194mⓘ Explain this passage (haiku)\u001b[39m                                                                       \u001b[20;55H\u001b[2mThis passage de\u001b[Ccribes\u001b[Cthe user interface\u001b[Cfor \"ask-mod\u001b[C exchanges\"\u001b[C(int\u001b[Cractions where the\u001b[Cuser\u001b[2Csks \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m     \u001b[21;55H\u001b[2mClaude ques\u001b[Ci\u001b[Cns about a d\u001b[Ccumen\u001b[C). B\u001b[Clow each\u001b[Cexchange, there are three clickable\u001b[Cbuttons that allow the\u001b[22;55Huser to exit or p\u001b[Coc\u001b[Ced from that interaction. These buttons\u001b[2Cre styl\u001b[Cd a\u001b[C simpl\u001b[C,\u001b[Cplain-looking controls \u001b[23;55Hrather \u001b[Chan elaborate or decorative elements, similar to how a pull request review interface provides \u001b[24;55Hstraightforward action options.\u001b[25;55H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38mdis\u001b[Ciss\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m83 out · 0 c\u001b[Cched\u001b[26;52H\u001b[39m \u001b[2C\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mcomment · ask · explain\u001b[39m    \u001b[C   \u001b[C \u001b[C   \u001b[C \u001b[C    \u001b[C \u001b[C      \u001b[C      \u001b[C        \u001b[27;57H\u001b[1mK\u001b[Cep\u001b[Cas\u001b[3Cmm\u001b[Cnt\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m: converts the Q and A\u001b[Cinto a pinned review comment.\u001b[28;52H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m·\u001b[2C\u001b[39m-\u001b[C\u001b[1mSend to conversation\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;2;38;38;38m: \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m$.prompt.submit\u001b[39m rig\u001b[Ct\u001b[Cn\u001b[Cw wi\u001b[Ch\u001b[Cthe\u001b[Cblock \u001b[Cs    \u001b[29;55H  hidden context, for when the user wants the model to act immediately. \u001b[33C \u001b[42;3H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
